# What the Android build talks to, and the only reason this file exists.
#
# Vite loads `.env.local` in EVERY mode, and it overrides `.env`. That file is
# where a developer keeps the address of a worker running on their own machine
# — which is correct for `npm run dev` and catastrophic in a package: a phone
# asked to reach `http://localhost:8787` reaches itself, so the board, the
# friends, the duels and the corporations all answer nothing, while the profile
# and the day quietly fall back to `localStorage` and look like they work.
#
# That is exactly what shipped in the first 1.1.1 build. A mode file beats
# `.env.local`, so naming the address here takes the question away from whatever
# happens to be on the machine at the time.
#
# No secret belongs in here. This file is committed on purpose — the address is
# public, it is in the shipped bundle already — and `.gitignore` covers `.env`
# and `.env*.local` but not this, which is the arrangement that makes the rule
# above enforceable rather than remembered.
VITE_API_URL=https://broker-stars-api.broker-stars-worker.workers.dev
